  "sources": [
    "Water towers use gravity to provide pressure; each foot of height adds about 0.43 psi (so about 2.3 ft per psi): https://www.ipm.org/amomentofscience/physics-water-towers/ ; https://www.waterworld.com/drinking-water/distribution/article/14287229/what-is-the-purpose-of-water-towers ; https://www.mentalfloss.com/article/64577/how-do-water-towers-work",
